---
// Bring-your-own-models proof: each agent on the plan or key you gave it.
---

<div
  class="tg-card tg"
  role="img"
  aria-label="Telegram message from klanker listing which model plan each agent runs on: clerk on a Claude plan login, marko on a Codex plan, coach on a local model, klanker on OpenRouter with its own key, and zero silent fallbacks to a metered API."
>
  <div class="tg-head" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="back">‹</span>
    <span class="who"><b>klanker</b><span>bot</span></span>
    <span class="tg-ava a4">k</span>
  </div>
  <div class="tg-body" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="msg out tail">
      <p>who's running on what?</p>
      <span class="meta">14:05 <span class="ticks">✓✓</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="msg in tail" style="max-width:92%">
      <span class="name">klanker</span>
      <p class="card-title">🔌 Model plans</p>
      <div class="rows">
        <span class="row"><span class="st ok">✓</span><span>clerk: <b>Claude</b> plan login</span></span>
        <span class="row"><span class="st ok">✓</span><span>marko: <b>Codex</b> plan</span></span>
        <span class="row"><span class="st ok">✓</span><span>coach: <b>local</b> model, your GPU</span></span>
        <span class="row"><span class="st ok">✓</span><span>klanker: <b>OpenRouter</b>, its own key</span></span>
        <span class="row"><span class="st ok">✓</span><span>Silent API fallbacks: <b>0</b></span></span>
      </div>
      <span class="meta">14:05</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
